n: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $471K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["GrafTech International Ltd. is a micro-cap industrials business with a $261M market cap on $504M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -27% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -7% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 25%.","The company is burning through $121M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 40% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 24% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on ca